-- title:
--   Bi-fibre degree count with graph defect for a compositum
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and let $F, F_1, F_2, E, M$ be fields equipped with $K$-algebra and $F$-algebra structures arranged in compatible towers $F \subseteq F_1, F_2 \subseteq E \subseteq M$ over $K$, with $F_1/F$, $F_2/F$, $E/F$, $E/F_1$, $E/F_2$ and $M/F$ finite and $M/F$ Galois; assume moreover an $F$- and $K$-compatible integral algebra map $F_2 \to F_1$ whose underlying ring map is surjective, hence an isomorphism $\theta$ of $F_2$ onto $F_1$ over $F$. Assume that the $F$-subalgebra of $E$ generated by the images of $F_1$ and $F_2$ is all of $E$, that $[E:F] + [F_1:F] = [F_1:F]\,[F_2:F]$, and that $[F_2:F] \neq 2$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, i.e. a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ whose valuation ring is a principal ideal ring, and let $w_1$, $w_2$ be places of $F_1$, $F_2$ whose valuation subrings contract to that of $v$. Let $T$ be a finite set of places of $E$ consisting exactly of those $W$ contracting to $w_1$ on $F_1$ and to $w_2$ on $F_2$. Here, for a place $W$ of a field $F'$ over $K$ and a subfield $F$, $e(W/F)$ denotes the least positive $n$ of the form $\mathrm{ord}_W(f)$ with $0 \neq f \in F$, and $f(W/F)$ the degree of the residue field of $W$ over that of its contraction to $F$. Then
--   $$\sum_{W \in T} e(W/F)\,f(W/F) \;+\; \begin{cases} e(w_1/F)\,f(w_1/F) & \text{if } w_1 \text{ contracts to } w_2 \text{ along } \theta,\\ 0 & \text{otherwise,}\end{cases} \;=\; e(w_1/F)\,f(w_1/F)\cdot e(w_2/F)\,f(w_2/F).$$
--
--   This is a defected form of the fundamental degree identity for the bi-fibre of a pair of places in a compositum: under the stated degree relation the algebra $F_1 \otimes_F F_2$ splits as $E$ together with the graph of the isomorphism $\theta$, and the extra term accounts for the graph component. It is used in the verification of the diagonal Hecke identity [`ModularCurve.heckeDiagonalIdentity_of_prime_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeDiagonalIdentity_of_prime_of_not_dvd).
